WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.235 --> 00:00:01.840
It's time for Drew's News.

2
00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:05.100
Your daily jiggle of that good news jello.

3
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.650
Whoa.
And with me at the desk...

4
00:00:06.650 --> 00:00:09.000
I can't say jello without doing this.

5
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.070
His favorite jello flavor is red.

6
00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.075
Rossi Ross Mathews.

7
00:00:12.075 --> 00:00:13.701
(audience cheers)
Jello.

8
00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:14.534
Jello.

9
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:20.820
First up, the hardest working woman in showbiz

10
00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:23.129
has done it again.

11
00:00:23.129 --> 00:00:25.737
NME reports, Madonna's new live concert film

12
00:00:25.737 --> 00:00:28.760
"Madame X" is out on Paramount Plus right now.

13
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.330
Cameras followed her on tour dates

14
00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:33.180 line:15%
for 75 days around the world,

15
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:35.130 line:15%
and I was lucky enough to be in the audience

16
00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.740 line:15%
for the New York premiere.

17
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:38.960 line:15%
Uh-huh, and I got to ask her a question.

18
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:39.793 line:15%
Madonna.

19
00:00:39.793 --> 00:00:40.740 line:15%
(Ross laughs)

20
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.930 line:15%
By the way, she would not approve of any of this goofiness.

21
00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:46.080 line:15%
I feel like she's so damn cool.

22
00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:48.290 line:15%
But I wanted to share the moment with you.

23
00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:50.080 line:15%
So take a look.

24
00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:55.080
My question for you was, have you said no to anything

25
00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.490
that you wish you had said yes to?

26
00:00:58.490 --> 00:01:00.240
And what was that thing?

27
00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.330
Ooh, that's a good one.
Good question.

28
00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:05.460
Yeah, I was given the script to "The Matrix."

29
00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:07.050
What?
I was offered

30
00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:09.473
the role of Trinity.

31
00:01:10.627 --> 00:01:11.651
You're kidding.

32
00:01:11.651 --> 00:01:12.820
I read the script and I'm like,

33
00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.957
this is the stupidest (beep) I've ever read in my life.

34
00:01:15.957 --> 00:01:16.800
What?

35
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:17.883
I turned it down.

36
00:01:19.701 --> 00:01:21.570
(audience laughing)
(Drew laughing)

37
00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:22.450
Okay.

38
00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:24.310
I'm sorry, do you know how cool it is

39
00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:25.700
that you get to go to opening night

40
00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.740
and you get to ask Madonna a question?

41
00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:30.200
The truth is I used to be all up in the club with Madonna

42
00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:31.450
and Sean back in the day.

43
00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:33.330
So I've really known her most of my life

44
00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:34.560
Of course.

45
00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.370
But, she's also still Madonna

46
00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:38.150
and I'm geeking out and freaking out.

47
00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:41.720
But this concert film is really unlike other concert films.

48
00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:44.110
It makes you feel like you've traveled to Europe,

49
00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:47.224
and you're seeing exquisite performance art.

50
00:01:47.224 --> 00:01:50.485
I felt like I had left the country

51
00:01:50.485 --> 00:01:52.760
and gone to some beautiful place.

52
00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:54.300
And she's wearing a black wig in it,

53
00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.050
and the people in it are just...

54
00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:58.340
It's really incredible.

55
00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:00.170
Yeah, I met Madonna one time.

56
00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:01.003
And?

57
00:02:01.003 --> 00:02:01.836
Yeah, mm-hmm.

58
00:02:01.836 --> 00:02:04.530
She goes like this and I like touched her hand,

59
00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:06.660
and I felt like I was touched for the very first time.

60
00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.560
(audience laughs)
(Drew laughs)

61
00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:10.600
You were, Rossi. You were.
I was.

62
00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:13.315
Well, okay, hey Drew, we've got a little follow-up for you.

63
00:02:13.315 --> 00:02:15.051
You remember earlier this week, if you were watching,

64
00:02:15.051 --> 00:02:17.611
we played a game of Chicago trivia,

65
00:02:17.611 --> 00:02:20.070
and it was Chicago native Ike Barinholtz

66
00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:23.920
versus Chicago Blackhawks' Jonathan Toews and Seth Jones.

67
00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.610 line:15%
The stakes were high, they did trivia,

68
00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:27.276 line:15%
and the loser agreed to be posted

69
00:02:27.276 --> 00:02:32.040 line:15%
on a huge Drew yellow billboard for all of Chicago to see.

70
00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:35.080 line:15%
And the loser kept their word.

71
00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:36.060 line:15%
Take a look at this.

72
00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.110 line:15%
I know. This is real.

73
00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:38.450 line:15%
This is not a mock up.

74
00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:40.343 line:15%
We love "The Drew Barrymore Show"

75
00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.009 line:15%
with the Chicago Blackhawks.

76
00:02:43.009 --> 00:02:45.270 line:15%
(audience cheering)

77
00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:46.900 line:15%
Guess what, Chicago?

78
00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.654 line:15%
We're coming for ya.

79
00:02:48.654 --> 00:02:50.220
Oh yeah.
Oh yeah.

80
00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.330
We're bringing the show to you.

81
00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:54.630
So watch out, 'cause we're coming to town soon.

82
00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:55.563
We love you.

83
00:02:55.563 --> 00:02:56.670
(Ross laughs)

84
00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:57.610
Chicago.

85
00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:58.731
Stay tuned for that.

86
00:02:58.731 --> 00:03:01.898 line:15%
(upbeat bright music)

